<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tournai</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Doornik, Tornacum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tournai is a city in the province of Hainaut in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>, and one of the oldest towns in the country. As Roman Tornacum it became the seat of the Salian Frankish kings in the 5th century; the tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childeric-i">Childeric I</a>, father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a>, was found there in 1653. Its Romanesque and Gothic Cathedral of Our Lady is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tournai.jpg" alt="Tournai" width="320" height="135" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: stephane martin · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Grand-Place_de_Tournai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
